```rust
fn fib(n: u32) -> Option<u128> {
    let mut a: u128 = 0; // F(0)
    let mut b: u128 = 1; // F(1)

    for _ in 0..n {
        let next = a.checked_add(b)?;
        a = b;
        b = next;
    }

    Some(a)
}
```

This returns `Some(F(n))` for `n = 0, 1, 2, ...`, and returns `None` as soon as the next Fibonacci number would overflow `u128`.
